WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
- Welcome back!

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:05.710
All right, we are celebrating
Pasta Week all week long,

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:07.630
that's why we call it Pasta Week.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:11.800
And what better way to pay
homage to the humble noodle

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.670
than a cookbook club pick

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:16.540
with my culinary partner in crime?

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.950
Today's pick comes from
the great Hetty McKinnon

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.430
and my culinary partner in crime

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.659
is the one and only Chef Pilar Valdes!

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:31.659
(audience applauds)
- Hi everyone.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.100
So today what we're doing

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.080
is a spicy Sesame Tantanmen Ramen

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.230
from Hetty McKinnon's
"To Asia, With Love."

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.330
I love that cookbook.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.570
All the recipes in this
book, "To Asia, With Love"

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:48.080
are actually vegetarian.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.690
The recipe we're making
today is actually vegan.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.380
So what you have there

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.880
is some Sesame oil with
some ginger and garlic

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.140
that's been sauteing,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:02.100
and then we're gonna throw
in our crumbled, firm tofu

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.700
into that mixture,

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.300
and it just smells so good.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.730
So we've mixed everything in,

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.960
and then Drew, to your side,

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.210
you're gonna have mirin,

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:17.200
which is a Japanese
rice wine, cooking wine,

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.160
and then we're gonna do a
little bit of tamari, as well,

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:25.030
and then we're gonna see
throw in the miso paste also.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:26.030
- I love miso paste.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:28.430
- [Pilar] So Drew, as soon
as you have that mixed in

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:29.780
really nicely,
- [Drew] Okay.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:31.103
- Nice and crumbled,

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:35.140
you're just gonna let it go
actually, and stop mixing it.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.210
And what that's gonna do

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.280
is basically develop
this nice, crispy crust

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.010
on the tofu as it cooks.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.640
So while that's cooking, I'm at a seven,

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:46.190
we're gonna make the sauce,

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:47.450
or the broth, basically.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.823
So in the bowl,

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:50.830
we're gonna whisk up a little,

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:52.700
in the bowl you have some tahini,

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.343
so we're gonna put a little
bit more of the tamari,

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:01.030
and that's gonna give you
again, that deep savoriness.

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:02.140
Lovely.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:06.530
And then, to a break up a
little bit of the creaminess,

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.060
you're gonna have a little
bit of the rice wine vinegar

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.180
in that bowl.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.223
Oh, that's starting to look really nice.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.340
And then we have some chili oil.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:20.290
So as soon as you're all mixed in, Drew,

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:23.410
we're gonna walk over to
the big pot over here,

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:27.320
and in this pot we have
some vegetable stock

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.250
and some soy milk.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.320
So that's, again, the creaminess,

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:33.740
you're just building that in.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.340
If you don't wanna do soy milk,

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.310
you can absolutely substitute

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:41.650
for any of your favorite
nut milks, basically.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.590
And you're gonna whisk that in, Drew.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.870
I'm gonna ch check my, ooh,

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.550
so you can see,

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.300
I'm getting all this texture,

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.560
you have a little bit of crispy, crunchy,

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.040
and then the softness too,

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.143
and that's exactly where you want it.

00:02:57.055 --> 00:02:58.700
All right, I'm gonna pop that off.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:02:59.533
And then, Drew,

00:02:59.533 --> 00:03:03.330
I think we're ready to
assemble our ramen bowl.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.260
- [Drew] Great.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.970
- All right, so what Hetty says

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.590
is basically cook your
favorite ramen noodle,

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:11.200
according to the package instructions,

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.720
and then in the last 30 seconds,

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:15.900
into the water, throw your vegetable.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.070
So here we have some leafy greens

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.730
and some bean sprouts,

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:22.690
so you really just wanna
shock the raw off of it,

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:23.620
but you still want it

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.970
to be crunchy.
- I love it.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:28.600
- Nice and fresh, so shall we assemble?

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:29.530
- Yes, please.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:30.470
- Yes, let's do it.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:33.520
All right, so you have
your cooked ramen noodles.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:34.353
- Cooked.

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.203
- A little bit of greens.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:42.100
I know you love your
beans sprouts too, right?

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.250
- I love beans sprouts.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.183
I love crunch.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.980
I need texture.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:51.260
- And then we've got
some, speaking of texture,

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.820
some sweet corn, as well.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:55.070
- I love that touch.

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:58.970
- So that's gonna be a
real nice pop of freshness,

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:01.400
'cause she to keep the kernels raw.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:05.270
And then your tofu, lest we forget,

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:07.080
lest we forget.
(audience applauds)

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.040
So I'm pouring my nice broth over here,

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.420
treating myself to something real special.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.280
And then we got your garnish.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.750
We got some Sesame seeds,
toasted Sesame seeds,

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:18.960
a little bit of scallion.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.300
- Is this a Szechuan chili crisp?

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:24.200
- And then it's more
chili crisp, basically.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.293
We did say it was gonna be hot.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.010
And there you have it.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:34.010
It's Hetty McKinnon's Spicy
Sesame Tantanmen Ramen.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.603
- Love it, it's so beautiful.

00:04:36.603 --> 00:04:39.603
(audience applauds)

00:04:40.615 --> 00:04:41.948
- [Both] Cheers!

00:04:43.135 --> 00:04:45.620
- Oh, Pilar, I love you so much.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:49.228
Thank you for bringing this to the table.

00:04:49.228 --> 00:04:52.728
(audience applauds)
- Mmm!

00:04:54.341 --> 00:04:55.174
- Mmm.

00:04:56.547 --> 00:04:57.690
Oh my God, Pilar.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:58.523
- That is so good.

00:04:58.523 --> 00:05:00.320
- It just made me weak in the knees.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.230
- That is so, so good.

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:03.400
- Like a man!

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.060
- I need to go in.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.533
- A man hasn't made me weak in the knees

00:05:07.533 --> 00:05:08.470
(Pilar laughs)

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.320
like this ramen has.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.190
I need to date this ramen.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:13.605
- Thank you, Hetty.

00:05:13.605 --> 00:05:14.960
(Pilar laughs)

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.750
You can pick up a copy of
our recommended cookbook

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.160
or get the full recipe at the website,

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.300
TheDrewBarrymoreShow.com.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.370
- And thank you, Pilar,

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:27.533
for bringing this pick to the week.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.287
And we be right back.

00:05:31.287 --> 00:05:33.870
(upbeat music)

